items.fromString:
There is a problem in this section:
[https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/red_hat_lightspeed/1-latest/html/using_apis_to_configure_red_hat_lightspeed_services/apis-authentication#generating-offline-access-token|https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/red_hat_lightspeed/1-latest/html/using_apis_to_configure_red_hat_lightspeed_services/apis-authentication#generating-offline-access-token]

The following curl command is provided:

{noformat}curl https://sso.redhat.com/auth/realms/redhat-external/protocol/openidconnect/token -d grant_type=refresh_token -d client_id=rhsm-api -d refresh_token=<offline_token>{noformat}

Trying to run it returns error:

{noformat}{
  "error": "Protocol not found"
}{noformat}

The problem is with the URL - the *openidconnect* part of it should be *openid-connect*, with the dash in the middle.

Reference:
[https://developers.redhat.com/cheat-sheets/red-hat-lightspeed-api-cheat-sheet|https://developers.redhat.com/cheat-sheets/red-hat-lightspeed-api-cheat-sheet]

items.toString:
There is a problem in this section:
[https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/red_hat_lightspeed/1-latest/html/using_apis_to_configure_red_hat_lightspeed_services/apis-authentication#apis-configuring-service-accounts|https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/red_hat_lightspeed/1-latest/html/using_apis_to_configure_red_hat_lightspeed_services/apis-authentication#apis-configuring-service-accounts]

The following curl command is provided:

{noformat}curl https://sso.redhat.com/auth/realms/redhat-external/protocol/openidconnect/token -d "grant_type=client_credentials" -d "scope=api.console" -d client_id=<client_id> -d client_secret=<client_secret>{noformat}

Trying to run it returns error:

{noformat}{
  "error": "Protocol not found"
}{noformat}

The problem is with the URL - the *openidconnect* part of it should be *openid-connect*, with the dash in the middle.

Similar problem in another curl command in:
[https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/red_hat_lightspeed/1-latest/html/using_apis_to_configure_red_hat_lightspeed_services/apis-authentication#generating-offline-access-token|https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/red_hat_lightspeed/1-latest/html/using_apis_to_configure_red_hat_lightspeed_services/apis-authentication#generating-offline-access-token]

Reference:
[https://developers.redhat.com/cheat-sheets/red-hat-lightspeed-api-cheat-sheet|https://developers.redhat.com/cheat-sheets/red-hat-lightspeed-api-cheat-sheet]

